WEBVTT

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.833
Pause the video to figure it out yourself.

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:32.533
Answer in 3

00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:35.063
Answer in 2

00:01:35.063 --> 00:01:37.673
Answer in 1

00:01:37.673 --> 00:01:41.745
It’s possible to calculate the exact 
probability of going free

00:01:41.745 --> 00:01:43.875
in all 100 spots.

00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:46.605
But there’s a much simpler path 
to the solution

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:49.765
that requires surprisingly
little calculation.

00:01:49.765 --> 00:01:52.315
Imagine being anywhere in line.

00:01:52.315 --> 00:01:56.406
Way up at the front, one of the three
heads will pick someone at random,

00:01:56.406 --> 00:01:59.896
and you’ll move forward 1, 2, or 3 spaces.

00:01:59.896 --> 00:02:02.226
Since each is equally likely,